{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-796bba08-932f-4990-8783-33c7eddcb3bd-25\nfc_849d619e-9aa2-9f4c-aefe-69e6b30c731f_0","tool_call":{"readToolCall":{"args":{"path":"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py","offset":3460,"limit":210},"result":{"success":{"content":"\n                    etype, payload = parse_opencode_event(event)\n                    if etype == \"reasoning\":\n                        rtext = payload.get(\"reasoning_content\")\n                        if isinstance(rtext, str):\n                            rtext = _strip_interrupted(rtext)\n                            if rtext:\n                                payload[\"reasoning_content\"] = rtext\n                            else:\n                                del payload[\"reasoning_content\"]\n                        if payload:\n                            attempt_output = True\n                            if isinstance(rtext, str) and rtext:\n                                attempt_reasonings.append(rtext)\n                            chunk_str = format_sse_chunk(resp_id, created, shown_model, payload)\n                            self.wfile.write(chunk_str.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n                            self.wfile.flush()\n                    elif etype == \"text\":\n                        ttext = payload.get(\"content\")\n                        if isinstance(ttext, str):\n                            ttext = _strip_interrupted(ttext)\n                        if isinstance(ttext, str) and ttext:\n                            attempt_output = True\n                            if retries and not incomplete_retry and not attempt_texts and collected_texts:\n                                emit_content(\"\\n\\n\")\n                            attempt_texts.append(ttext)\n                            if parser is not None:\n                                parser.feed(ttext)\n                            else:\n                                emit_content(ttext)\n                    elif etype == \"step_finish\":\n                        if payload:\n                            for key in (\"input\", \"output\", \"cached\", \"reasoning\"):\n                                usage[key] = int(usage.get(key) or 0) + int(payload.get(key) or 0)\n                            attempt_output_tokens += int(payload.get(\"output\") or 0)\n                            attempt_reasoning_tokens += int(payload.get(\"reasoning\") or 0)\n                        if emulate_tools and tool_calls:\n                            # Следующие шаги — реакция на «отклонение» (повтор вызова): не нужны.\n                            _log(\"stream: step with tool call finished, stopping opencode run\")\n                            _stop_proc(proc)\n                            break\n                    elif etype == \"error\":\n                        _log(f\"stream provider error: HTTP {payload.get('statusCode')}: {payload.get('message')}\")\n                        if isinstance(payload.get(\"statusCode\"), int):\n                            provider_status = payload[\"statusCode\"]\n                        err_lines.append(f\"HTTP {payload.get('statusCode')}: {payload.get('message')}\")\n                        if attempt_output:\n                            # Оборванный ответ: иначе opencode сам запустит SYNTHETIC-шаг «Continue…» —\n                            # останавливаем сразу. Транзиентная ошибка -> повтор шага, детерминированная\n                            # (401…) -> ошибка клиенту без повтора. Ошибка до первого токена — не трогаем:\n                            # opencode повторит сам или выйдет, и тогда флаг не должен «залипнуть».\n                            if _is_transient_stream_error(payload):\n                                had_provider_error = True\n                            else:\n                                fatal_mid_error = True\n                            _log(f\"stream: provider error mid-response (transient={had_provider_error}), \"\n                                 \"stopping opencode run\")\n                            stopped_on_error = True\n                            _stop_proc(proc)\n                            break\n                        _log(\"stream: early provider error (waiting for CLI recovery)\")\n                    elif etype == \"tool_use\":\n                        attempt_output = True\n                        part = _dict_or_empty(event.get(\"part\"))\n                        tstate = _dict_or_empty(part.get(\"state\"))\n                        calls = (_native_to_tool_calls(part.get(\"tool\"), tstate.get(\"input\"), tools or [])\n                                 if emulate_tools else [])\n                        _log(f\"opencode built-in tool event: tool={part.get('tool')} status={tstate.get('status')} \"\n                             f\"mapped={bool(calls)} as={[c['name'] for c in calls]}\")\n                        if calls:\n                            if parser is not None:\n                                parser.finish()\n                            for call in calls:\n                                emit_tool_call(call)\n                        elif emulate_tools:\n                            unmapped.append(str(part.get(\"tool\")))\n\n                if feed.overflowed:\n                    # Читатель уже остановил процесс (stdout_overflow): попытка неуспешна, данные не дропаются молча.\n                    had_provider_error = True\n                    stopped_on_error = True\n                    err_lines.append(\"stdout queue overflow\")\n                timed_out = feed.timed_out\n                if timed_out:\n                    _log(f\"stream timeout after {TIMEOUT_S:.0f}s, killing proc group\")\n                    _stop_proc(proc)\n\n                try:\n                    proc.wait(timeout=15)\n                except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n                    try:\n                        proc.kill()\n                    except OSError:\n                        pass\n\n                err_thread.join(timeout=5)\n                feed.join(timeout=5)\n                if parser is not None:\n                    parser.finish()\n                prefix_dedup = dedup[0]\n                dedup[0] = None\n                if prefix_dedup is not None:\n                    leftover = prefix_dedup.finish()\n                    if leftover:\n                        send_text(leftover)\n                feed.close()\n                try:\n                    if proc.stderr is not None:\n                        proc.stderr.close()\n                except OSError:\n                    pass\n\n                gate.release()\n                rc = proc.returncode if proc.returncode is not None else -1\n                if stopped_on_error and rc < 0:\n                    rc = 1  # остановили сами после ошибки провайдера: для классификации отказа — как выход CLI\n                tail = _clean_err(err_lines[-6:])\n                transient_failure = had_provider_error or (\n                    not attempt_output and _is_retryable_failure(rc, tail, provider_status, False))\n                attempts.attempt_done(transient_failure, attempt_output and not transient_failure)\n                if timed_out:\n                    failure = {\"rc\": rc, \"tail\": \"\", \"timeout\": True}\n                    break\n                if rc != 0 and not attempt_output:\n                    _log(f\"stream cli failed rc={rc} stderr_tail={tail!r}\")\n                    if (fail_retries < FAIL_RETRY_LIMIT and time.monotonic() < deadline\n                            and _is_retryable_failure(rc, tail, provider_status, bool(tool_calls))\n                            and attempts.allow_retry(\"cli_failure\", charge_budget=provider_status is not None)):\n                        fail_retries += 1\n                        _log(f\"stream retry {fail_retries}/{FAIL_RETRY_LIMIT} after cli failure without output\")\n                        continue\n                    if not collected_texts and not tool_calls:\n                        failure = {\"rc\": rc, \"tail\": tail}\n                        break\n\n                if fatal_mid_error and not tool_calls:\n                    failure = {\"rc\": rc, \"tail\": tail, \"partial\": True}\n                    break\n                if not emulate_tools or tool_calls or time.monotonic() > deadline:\n                    break\n                if unmapped:\n                    if unmapped_retries >= NATIVE_RETRY_LIMIT or not attempts.allow_retry(\"unmapped\"):\n                        _log(f\"stream unmapped built-in tools={unmapped}: retries exhausted ({unmapped_retries})\")\n                        emit_content(f\"\\n\\n[opencode-zen-bridge: модель вызывала недоступный встроенный \"\n                                     f\"инструмент ({', '.join(unmapped)}); повторы исчерпаны]\")\n                        break\n                    retries += 1\n                    unmapped_retries += 1\n                    incomplete_retry = False\n                    _log(f\"stream unmapped built-in tools={unmapped}: re-prompt \"\n                         f\"{unmapped_retries}/{NATIVE_RETRY_LIMIT}\")\n                    attempt_prompt = _rewrite_tool_tags_for_model(_unavailable_tools_prompt(\n                        attempt_prompt, \"\".join(attempt_texts), unmapped, tools or [], model), model)\n                    continue\n                signal = 0 if provider_status in _FATAL_HTTP else _incomplete_step_signal(\n                    \"\".join(attempt_texts), \"\".join(attempt_reasonings), tools or [],\n                    had_provider_error, attempt_output_tokens, attempt_reasoning_tokens,\n                    tool_choice=tool_choice)\n                if not signal:\n                    break\n                if incomplete_retries >= NATIVE_RETRY_LIMIT or not attempts.allow_retry(\"incomplete_step\"):\n                    _log(f\"stream incomplete tool step: retries exhausted ({incomplete_retries}) signal={signal}\")\n                    break\n                retries += 1\n                incomplete_retries += 1\n                incomplete_retry = True\n                attempts.signal = signal\n                _log(f\"stream incomplete tool step: re-prompt {incomplete_retries}/{NATIVE_RETRY_LIMIT} \"\n                     f\"signal={signal} total_spawns={attempts.total_spawns}/{attempts.max_total}\")\n                attempt_prompt = _rewrite_tool_tags_for_model(_incomplete_tool_step_prompt(\n                    prompt, \"\".join(collected_texts), tools or [], tool_choice, model), model)\n\n            if failure is not None:\n                _log(f\"stream failed model={model} rc={failure['rc']} fail_retries={fail_retries} \"\n                     f\"total_spawns={attempts.total_spawns}\")\n                if failure.get(\"timeout\"):\n                    xs[\"exit_reason\"] = \"timeout\"\n                    self._sse_error(_error_payload(f\"opencode timed out after {TIMEOUT_S:.0f}s\"))\n                    return\n                xs[\"exit_reason\"] = \"provider_fatal\" if failure.get(\"partial\") else \"upstream_failed\"\n                what = (\"opencode provider error after partial output\" if failure.get(\"partial\")\n                        else \"opencode run failed\")\n                self._sse_error(_error_payload(\n                    f\"{what} (rc={failure['rc']})\"\n                    + (\"\" if failure.get(\"partial\") else \" without output\")\n                    + (f\": {failure['tail']}\" if failure[\"tail\"] else \"\"), failure[\"tail\"]))\n                return\n\n            if dropped_blocks[0] and not tool_calls and not \"\".join(collected_texts).strip():\n                emit_content(_BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE)  # иначе клиент получил бы пустой ответ\n            full_text = \"\".join(collected_texts)\n            prompt_tokens = int(usage.get(\"input\") or 0) or _estimate_tokens(prompt)\n            completion_tokens = int(usage.get(\"output\") or 0) or _estimate_tokens(full_text)\n\n            final_chunk = format_sse_chunk(\n                resp_id,\n                created,\n                shown_model,\n                {},\n                finish_reason=\"tool_calls\" if tool_calls else \"stop\",\n                usage=_build_openai_usage(prompt_tokens, completion_tokens,\n                                          int(usage.get(\"cached\") or 0), int(usage.get(\"reasoning\") or 0)),\n            )\n            self.wfile.write(final_chunk.encode(\"utf-8\"))\n            self.wfile.write(b\"data: [DONE]\\n\\n\")\n            self.wfile.flush()\n            xs.update(exit_reason=\"ok\", tools=len(tool_calls), out_chars=len(full_text), rc=proc.returncode)\n            _log(f\"stream done model={model} rc={proc.returncode} tools={len(tool_calls)} \"\n                 f\"out_chars={len(full_text)} emulate_tools={emulate_tools} retries={retries} \"\n                 f\"total_spawns={attempts.total_spawns}\")","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":4022,"fileSize":200835,"path":"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py","readRange":{"startLine":3460,"endLine":3669},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-796bba08-932f-4990-8783-33c7eddcb3bd-25\nfc_849d619e-9aa2-9f4c-aefe-69e6b30c731f_0","startedAtMs":"1792866826976","completedAtMs":"1792866827558"},"model_call_id":"306f7807-0e37-4b19-beb8-40541a588c90-8-ndpv","session_id":"81f4d8b7-02cf-45e0-8b1e-62e9a8ce8268","timestamp_ms":1792866827684}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-796bba08-932f-4990-8783-33c7eddcb3bd-26\nfc_849d619e-9aa2-9f4c-aefe-69e6b30c731f_1","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"def _normalize_arguments","path":"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/core/tool_emulation.py","outputMode":"content","contextAfter":25,"caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-796bba08-932f-4990-8783-33c7eddcb3bd-26\nfc_849d619e-9aa2-9f4c-aefe-69e6b30c731f_1","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"def _normalize_arguments","path":"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/core/tool_emulation.py","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/.ai-team/runs/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix-20261024":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/core/tool_emulation.py","matches":[{"lineNumber":62,"content":"def _normalize_arguments(value: Any) -> dict | None:","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":63,"content":"    \"\"\"arguments -> JSON-объект; None, если значение задано, но объектом не является.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":64,"content":"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":65,"content":"    None отличает невалидные аргументы (строку-не-JSON, список, число, null) от","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":66,"content":"    отсутствия ключа: вызывающий код не вправе молча подменять их на пустой словарь","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":67,"content":"    и запускать инструмент с пустыми аргументами.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":68,"content":"    \"\"\"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":69,"content":"    if isinstance(value, dict):","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":70,"content":"        return value","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":71,"content":"    if isinstance(value, str):","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":72,"content":"        text = value.strip()","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":73,"content":"        if text:","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":74,"content":"            try:","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":75,"content":"                parsed = json.loads(text)","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":76,"content":"            except ValueError:","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":77,"content":"                return None","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":78,"content":"            if isinstance(parsed, dict):","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":79,"content":"                return parsed","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":80,"content":"    return None","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":81,"content":"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":82,"content":"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":83,"content":"def _normalize_tool_call(item: Any) -> dict:","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":84,"content":"    \"\"\"Один OpenAI tool_call -> {\"id\", \"name\", \"arguments\"}.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":85,"content":"","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":86,"content":"    id сохраняется, чтобы результат [tool result <id>] однозначно сопоставлялся","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true},{"lineNumber":87,"content":"    с конкретным вызовом при нескольких одинаковых инструментах.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":true}]}],"totalLines":26,"totalMatchedLines":1,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-796bba08-932f-4990-8783-33c7eddcb3bd-26\nfc_849d619e-9aa2-9f4c-aefe-69e6b30c731f_1","startedAtMs":"1792866827235","completedAtMs":"1792866827560"},"model_call_id":"306f7807-0e37-4b19-beb8-40541a588c90-8-ndpv","session_id":"81f4d8b7-02cf-45e0-8b1e-62e9a8ce8268","timestamp_ms":1792866827698}
{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"call-796bba08-932f-4990-8783-33c7eddcb3bd-27\nfc_849d619e-9aa2-9f4c-aefe-69e6b30c731f_2","tool_call":{"grepToolCall":{"args":{"pattern":"fails open|fail-closed|fail closed|STRIP_SCAN|in-code|markdown","path":"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/.ai-team/runs/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix-20261024","glob":"*.md","outputMode":"content","caseInsensitive":false,"multiline":false,"toolCallId":"call-796bba08-932f-4990-8783-33c7eddcb3bd-27\nfc_849d619e-9aa2-9f4c-aefe-69e6b30c731f_2","offset":0},"result":{"success":{"pattern":"fails open|fail-closed|fail closed|STRIP_SCAN|in-code|markdown","path":"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/.ai-team/runs/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix-20261024","outputMode":"content","workspaceResults":{"/Users/aazhiry1/tmp/cli-agent-bridge/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix/.ai-team/runs/opencode-zen-tool-invoke-fix-20261024":{"content":{"matches":[{"file":"./panel/council/r1/seats/1/brief.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":22,"content":"  - `_strip_broken_tool_blocks(text)` strips unparseable raw `<tool_call>`/`<tool_invoke>` blocks outside markdown code at 3 sinks (`Handler._stream_sse`, `Handler._serve_json`, `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`) and emits `_BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE` when nothing else is visible.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":23,"content":"  - Per `ARCH_PANEL` Skeptic (`k=1`), when a 17th candidate outside markdown code is reached (`scanned >= _STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16`), `_strip_broken_tool_blocks` fails closed by dropping `text[start:]` and logging `tool_strip_cap_hit max=16 dropping tail`, guaranteeing 0 leaked broken tags even on pathological input while bounding CPU to $O(16 \\cdot n)$.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/council/r1/seats/3/brief.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":22,"content":"  - `_strip_broken_tool_blocks(text)` strips unparseable raw `<tool_call>`/`<tool_invoke>` blocks outside markdown code at 3 sinks (`Handler._stream_sse`, `Handler._serve_json`, `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`) and emits `_BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE` when nothing else is visible.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":23,"content":"  - Per `ARCH_PANEL` Skeptic (`k=1`), when a 17th candidate outside markdown code is reached (`scanned >= _STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16`), `_strip_broken_tool_blocks` fails closed by dropping `text[start:]` and logging `tool_strip_cap_hit max=16 dropping tail`, guaranteeing 0 leaked broken tags even on pathological input while bounding CPU to $O(16 \\cdot n)$.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/council/r1/seats/2/brief.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":22,"content":"  - `_strip_broken_tool_blocks(text)` strips unparseable raw `<tool_call>`/`<tool_invoke>` blocks outside markdown code at 3 sinks (`Handler._stream_sse`, `Handler._serve_json`, `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`) and emits `_BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE` when nothing else is visible.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":23,"content":"  - Per `ARCH_PANEL` Skeptic (`k=1`), when a 17th candidate outside markdown code is reached (`scanned >= _STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16`), `_strip_broken_tool_blocks` fails closed by dropping `text[start:]` and logging `tool_strip_cap_hit max=16 dropping tail`, guaranteeing 0 leaked broken tags even on pathological input while bounding CPU to $O(16 \\cdot n)$.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./teamlead/package.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":9,"content":"  - `REQ-002` (`AD-002`): `_strip_broken_tool_blocks` (with fail-closed tail truncation on the 17th candidate outside markdown code per `ARCH_PANEL` Skeptic `k=1`) strips unparseable raw `<tool_call>`/`<tool_invoke>` blocks at 3 sinks (`Handler._stream_sse`, `Handler._serve_json`, `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`), emitting `_BROKEN_BLOCK_NOTICE` only when nothing else is visible, while keeping `_split_tool_calls` and `_is_incomplete_tool_step` untouched.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":171,"content":"+_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16  # граница CPU: `_code_context` — O(len) на кандидата","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":178,"content":"+    Валидные блоки (одиночный, пачка без промежуточных закрытий), теги в markdown-коде","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":180,"content":"+    Незакрытый хвост и закрытый невалидный блок отбрасываются. После `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS`","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":181,"content":"+    кандидатов остаток отбрасывается целиком (fail-closed): битый тег не утекает ни при каком вводе.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":198,"content":"+            if scanned >= _STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS:","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":200,"content":"+                    _log(f\"tool_strip_cap_hit max={_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS} dropping tail\")","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/arch/r1/seats/3/verdict.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":12,"content":"- **`AD-002` / `REQ-002` (Sink-level broken block stripping):** Архитектурно превосходит буквальный вариант из handoff (`held`-буфера в live [`_stream_sse`](file:///Users/aazhiry1/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py#L3171-L3590) уже нет — вместо него используется [`_PrefixDedup`](file:///Users/aazhiry1/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py#L1547-L1580)). Покусочная фильтрация в `emit_parsed_content` корректна относительно нарезки чанков в [`ToolCallParser._drain`](file:///Users/aazhiry1/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py#L2137-L2182): отклонённый закрытый блок эмитится целиком (`open_tag + inner + close_tag`), незакрытый хвост на `finish()` начинается с `open_tag`, а markdown-цитированный тег (`verdict == \"quoted\"`) отдаётся голым открывающим тегом без `{` и не задевается `_RAW_CALL_RE`. Неприкосновенность [`_split_tool_calls`](file:///Users/aazhiry1/.dsh/bridges/opencode-zen-bridge/server.py#L2244-L2265) сохраняет `F-07`, а чтение сырых `attempt_texts` / `out[\"text [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":23,"content":"- **`H-CPU/v1`:** `raw_decode` вызывается исключительно на холодном пути отказа `json.loads`; в `_strip_broken_tool_blocks` потенциальная квадратичность `O(k * n)` от `_code_context` жёстко ограничена константой `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16` (линейная асимптотика `O(n)` с fail-open и логом).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/arch/r1/seats/2/verdict.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":11,"content":"**AD-002 / REQ-002.** Откладывать `held` нельзя: на live буфера нет, сырой тег идёт `emit_content → _PrefixDedup → send_text → collected_texts` и в re-prompt. Обёртка колбэка `ToolCallParser` в `_stream_sse`, strip сразу после `_split_tool_calls` в `_serve_json` и повторный strip в `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt` дают один инвариант на SSE и JSON, на обоих базовых деревьях. `_split_tool_calls` и семантика emit парсера остаются, поэтому `test_negative_control_garbage_still_text_and_logged` и `test_unparsed_block_returned_as_text` остаются зелёными на API парсера. `_is_incomplete_tool_step` читает сырые `attempt_texts`, ретраи и `MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS` не сдвигаются. Кусок «один emit = open+inner+close» проверен зондом на устаревшем снимке (EVD-005), не на `5f6b7cb0`; доказательством будет прогон новых stream-тестов уже после step 0 на перебазированной копии. Ветка `parser is None` сознательно вне фикса. Потолок `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16` — fail-open: 17-й битый тег может остаться в тексте. Д [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/arch/r1/seats/1/verdict.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":5,"content":"Скептик, k=1. Главный блокирующий дефект: AD-002 декларирует бюджет REQ-002 «ноль утёкших сырых тегов» и меру QA-001 «0 raw `<tool_call>/<tool_invoke>` в SSE/JSON/re-prompt», но `_strip_broken_tool_blocks` при `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16` сознательно fail-open: 17-й битый блок проходит во все три sink-а, включая `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`, то есть ровно воспроизводит исходный инцидент на патологичном вводе. Это не остаточный RISK-002 низкого impact, а прямое противоречие критерию приёмки; нужен fail-closed хвост (обрезать остаток от 17-го кандидата + notice + лог) либо честное ослабление REQ-002. VER-003/VER-004 дыру не закрывают: `-k broken_block` не требует кейса «17+ битых блоков», а `test_strip_scan_is_bounded` из тест-плана в замороженную поверхность VER-001..VER-004 по имени не попадает. [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":11,"content":"H-CPU/v1: VER-004 меряет одиночный 60 KiB блок (<5 мс, прототип 0.23/1.97 мс), но худший случай дизайна — 16 кандидатов × O(n) `_code_context` + повторный `_parse_tool_call_blocks` на истории 256 KiB при 8 параллельных ходах — ни одним VER не гейтится. VER-001 адекватен для core/muse; VER-002 с «failure set == baseline» зависит от честности записи baseline при re-baseline на live, который, по Q-A, прямо сейчас редактирует другая сессия: sha-guard в AD-004 без лока — это TOCTOU, а тяжёлый путь (живой ход на :9883) остался прозой §9, а не VER. Итог: каркас AD-001..AD-004 и C-MULT/S-HERD/R-BULK обоснования принимаю, но до Coder требуются: fail-closed поведение за капом 16 либо пересмотр REQ-002, тест 17+ блоков и худшего случая H-CPU в VER-003/VER-004, явная фиксация границы доверия для исполняемых восстановленных вызовов. [... omitted end of long line]","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/arch/r1/seats/1/brief.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":20,"content":"- **AD-002 (Sink-level broken block stripping):** Pure helper `_strip_broken_tool_blocks(text) -> tuple[str, int]` (capped at `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16` candidates for `H-CPU/v1` $O(n)$ bound) strips unparseable raw `<tool_call>`/`<tool_invoke>` blocks outside markdown code at 3 sinks: (1) `ToolCallParser` content callback in `Handler._stream_sse`, (2) `Handler._serve_json` after `_split_tool_calls`, and (3) `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`. `_split_tool_calls` itself is untouched so `test_negative_control_garbage_still_text_and_logged` and `test_unparsed_block_returned_as_text` stay 100% green. `_is_incomplete_tool_step` still inspects raw `attempt_texts` so retry triggers and caps (`MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS = 3`) are preserved.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/arch/r1/seats/2/brief.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":20,"content":"- **AD-002 (Sink-level broken block stripping):** Pure helper `_strip_broken_tool_blocks(text) -> tuple[str, int]` (capped at `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16` candidates for `H-CPU/v1` $O(n)$ bound) strips unparseable raw `<tool_call>`/`<tool_invoke>` blocks outside markdown code at 3 sinks: (1) `ToolCallParser` content callback in `Handler._stream_sse`, (2) `Handler._serve_json` after `_split_tool_calls`, and (3) `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`. `_split_tool_calls` itself is untouched so `test_negative_control_garbage_still_text_and_logged` and `test_unparsed_block_returned_as_text` stay 100% green. `_is_incomplete_tool_step` still inspects raw `attempt_texts` so retry triggers and caps (`MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS = 3`) are preserved.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/arch/r1/seats/3/brief.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":20,"content":"- **AD-002 (Sink-level broken block stripping):** Pure helper `_strip_broken_tool_blocks(text) -> tuple[str, int]` (capped at `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16` candidates for `H-CPU/v1` $O(n)$ bound) strips unparseable raw `<tool_call>`/`<tool_invoke>` blocks outside markdown code at 3 sinks: (1) `ToolCallParser` content callback in `Handler._stream_sse`, (2) `Handler._serve_json` after `_split_tool_calls`, and (3) `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`. `_split_tool_calls` itself is untouched so `test_negative_control_garbage_still_text_and_logged` and `test_unparsed_block_returned_as_text` stay 100% green. `_is_incomplete_tool_step` still inspects raw `attempt_texts` so retry triggers and caps (`MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS = 3`) are preserved.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./panel/arch/r1/seats/1.failed-1/brief.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":20,"content":"- **AD-002 (Sink-level broken block stripping):** Pure helper `_strip_broken_tool_blocks(text) -> tuple[str, int]` (capped at `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16` candidates for `H-CPU/v1` $O(n)$ bound) strips unparseable raw `<tool_call>`/`<tool_invoke>` blocks outside markdown code at 3 sinks: (1) `ToolCallParser` content callback in `Handler._stream_sse`, (2) `Handler._serve_json` after `_split_tool_calls`, and (3) `_incomplete_tool_step_prompt`. `_split_tool_calls` itself is untouched so `test_negative_control_garbage_still_text_and_logged` and `test_unparsed_block_returned_as_text` stay 100% green. `_is_incomplete_tool_step` still inspects raw `attempt_texts` so retry triggers and caps (`MAX_TOTAL_SPAWNS = 3`) are preserved.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]},{"file":"./architecture/arch-spec.md","matches":[{"lineNumber":112,"content":"Why a piece-level sink filter is sound (verified by probe, packet `EVD-005`): when a closed block is rejected `ToolCallParser._drain` calls `_emit(open_tag + inner + close_tag)` once; an unclosed tail at EOF is `_flush_all()` of a buffer that already starts at the open tag; a markdown-quoted tag is emitted as the bare tag (no `{`) and never matches `_RAW_CALL_RE`. Parsed blocks are never emitted as content.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":206,"content":"_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16     # H-CPU bound: _code_context is O(len) per candidate","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":213,"content":"2. Iterate candidates with `_RAW_CALL_RE.search(text, pos)`; at most `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS` candidates, beyond that stop and keep the remainder untouched (fail-open, log once).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":214,"content":"3. Candidate in markdown code (`_code_context(text, start, True) != \"text\"`) → keep the open tag literally, continue after it.","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false},{"lineNumber":266,"content":"- `_strip_broken_tool_blocks`: fast path O(n) search; slow path O(k·n) because `_code_context` is O(n) per candidate ⇒ **k capped at `_STRIP_SCAN_MAX_TAGS = 16`** (worst case ≤ 16·n; one 60 KiB broken block measured 1.97 ms; the capped worst case is covered by `test_strip_scan_is_bounded`). Remainder beyond the cap is left untouched (fail-open).","contentTruncated":false,"isContextLine":false}]}],"totalLines":27,"totalMatchedLines":27,"clientTruncated":false,"ripgrepTruncated":false}}}}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"call-796bba08-932f-4990-8783-33c7eddcb3bd-27\nfc_849d619e-9aa2-9f4c-aefe-69e6b30c731f_2","startedAtMs":"1792866827328","completedAtMs":"1792866827694"},"model_call_id":"306f7807-0e37-4b19-beb8-40541a588c90-8-ndpv","session_id":"81f4d8b7-02cf-45e0-8b1e-62e9a8ce8268","timestamp_ms":1792866827829}
